menuconfig CONFIG_MODULE
	bool "Whizz Studio Configuration Module"
	depends on TCP_SERVER
	select JSON_LIBRARY
	select RTC
	select I2C
	help
	  High-level configuration protocol handler that sits on top of the
	  tcp_server library. Owns the full TCP configuration flow: connection
	  timer, JSON packet decode/encode for MTP 03/04/05/06, field range
	  validation, and the application-facing CFG_Init / CFG_Resp / callback
	  API. The application never calls tcp_server functions directly.

if CONFIG_MODULE

config CFG_MODULE_CONN_TIMEOUT_MS
	int "Connection session timeout in milliseconds"
	default 30000
	help
	  After a client successfully completes the Security Sequence
	  handshake, a countdown timer starts. If no JSON packet is received
	  within this window, the Configuration Module forcibly disconnects
	  the client and fires CFG_EVT_CONN_TIMEOUT.
	  Set to 0 to disable the connection timer entirely (not recommended
	  for production use - use keepalive alone in that case).
	  The final value is not fixed; adjust via Kconfig overlay.

config CFG_MODULE_TX_BUF_SIZE
	int "Transmit JSON buffer size in bytes"
	default 512
	help
	  Size of the stack-local buffer used to build outbound JSON packets
	  (MTP 04 Read Response and MTP 01 ACK/NACK). Must be large enough
	  for the biggest response you expect (section M with all string fields
	  at maximum length is roughly 200 bytes; 512 gives comfortable margin).
	  Must not exceed CONFIG_TCP_SERVER_MAX_FRAME_SIZE.

module = CONFIG_MODULE
module-str = Configuration Module
source "subsys/logging/Kconfig.template.log_config"

endif # CONFIG_MODULE
